INT. PLANETARIUM DOME - NIGHT

A hushed hemisphere. A painted sky of stars wheels overhead. A single projector hums at the center on a pedestal.

OTTAVIA LINDO, 30s, in a velvet jacket, stands at the control console. RAFFERTY "RAFF" OBUYA, 30s, sits in the front row of reclining seats with a paper bag of takeout.

OTTAVIA
Raff, you're not supposed to be in here.

RAFF
I brought dumplings.

OTTAVIA
That's not an excuse.

RAFF
It's a bribe.

She sighs and turns the dome to a deep midnight blue. He lies back in the chair. The stars brighten.

RAFF (CONT'D)
Show me the Southern Cross.

OTTAVIA
You can't see it from here.

RAFF
Show me anyway.

She taps a key. A cluster of stars swells in the south. He lifts the bag and shakes it.

OTTAVIA
Five minutes. Then you leave.

RAFF
Come sit.

OTTAVIA
Raff--

RAFF
Ottavia.

She stops. She crosses the aisle and lowers herself into the seat beside him. They lie back together under the painted sky.

OTTAVIA
I'm sorry about Sunday.

RAFF ^
I'm sorry about Sunday.

They both laugh. The Southern Cross turns slowly overhead.

RAFF (CONT'D)
Ottavia, I got the job in Perth.

She stiffens. She turns her head toward him.

OTTAVIA
Of course you did.

RAFF
I haven't said yes.

OTTAVIA
Then say no.

RAFF
Ask me to.

The projector hums. She stares at the false stars for a long time. Then she takes his hand.

OTTAVIA
Don't go, Raff.
